This folder holds shim.cpp, s68k's own C interface to Moira,
https://github.com/dirkwhoffmann/Moira, for the `moira` feature's differential
harness (src/conformance/moira.rs, src/test/differential.rs). No part of
Moira's source is in this repository: scripts/fetch-moira.sh fetches it into
tests/moira/fetched, which git ignores, at commit
ce28239b0507ebfe1bf2ad2b9c9252dc2f2cc031 (2026-09-23), and build.rs copies its
core, Moira/, into the build's own folder, sets its configuration for a 68010
that counts its cycles as the hardware does (MOIRA_PRECISE_TIMING true,
MOIRA_MIMIC_MUSASHI false, MOIRA_EMULATE_ADDRESS_ERROR true) and compiles it
with the shim, for the host's tests only. Nothing fetches or compiles it
without the feature.

What it is used for
-------------------

Moira's 68010 counts its cycles bus access by bus access and is checked
against Toni Wilen's cputester on the hardware, loop mode included. It is the
reference of the 68010 dialect's cycles: every first word s68k decodes as a
68010 instruction is run from random states by both, one instruction each, and
the registers, memory and cycles compared, and every one-word instruction in a
one-instruction `dbf` loop, step by step, for loop mode. The 68010's timing
table in src/machine/timing.rs takes Moira's values where the 68000 User's
Manual gives a maximum or departs from it, and says which.

